ubclass's built-in value; a bound method of a Python"] [100 2 "// function is called by pushing its frame"] [132 1 "// dictArgs are a keyword dictionary as a call's trailing keyword arguments."] [219 20 "// a dict subclass's __setitem__ sees the body's names (PY5e, part 2b)"] [250 1 "// updateBases resolves __mro_entries__ (PEP 560): the same tuple when no base has one."] [291 1 "// calculateMetaclass is _PyType_CalculateMetaclass: the most derived of meta and the bases' types."] [308 1 "// ---- type.__new__, type.__init__, type.__call__ ----"] [389 3 "// type_ready_set_dict's gh-55664"] [400 2 "// type_new_set_attrs comes before PyType_Ready: a metaclass's mro() sees __class__ set"] [407 2 "// __module__, __qualname__, __doc__"] [426 2 "// __new__ a staticmethod, __init_subclass__ and __class_getitem__ classmethods"] [435 2 "// __slots__ (type_new_slots)"] [454 32 "// type_dict_set_doc; a member named __doc__ is there already (typing's _SpecialForm)"] [456 2 "// __eq__ without __hash__ makes the class unhashable"] [464 2 "// __set_name__"] [476 2 "// __init_subclass__: super(type, type), whose check reads the MRO (a custom mro() may have left the class out)"] [498 1 "// checkLayouts refuses bases whose instance layouts conflict."] [509 1 "// bestBase is best_base: the base whose solid base is the most derived."] [527 1 "// c3MRO is the C3 linearization of t over its bases (mro_internal's mro_implementation)."] [589 1 "// mangle is _Py_Mangle: __x in class C is _C__x."] [612 1 "// ---- object.__new__, object.__init__ ----"] [614 1 "// overrides is a heap class of t's MRO defining name, or, for __new__, t's built-in solid base not"] [615 1 "// object (a built-in type's inherited slot cannot be told from its own: Go's functions do not compare)."] [626 4 "// a static type's tp_name is its module's and its name (select.poll)"] [672 25 "// its __del__ at its death (finalize.go, queue 218)"] [691 2 "// The data model's slots of object and type (REQUEST to PY5b: leave these to class.go)."] [704 1 "// ---- the slots of a class (fixup_slot_dispatchers, update_slot) ----"] [710 1 "// pyDefined is name defined by a heap class of t's MRO (a Python method), and its value."] [719 1 "// fixupSlots fills t's slots: the built-in solid base's (unwrapping a built-in subclass's value),"] [720 1 "// then a dispatcher for each special method a class of the MRO defines. Rerun on a class's"] [721 1 "// special attribute's assignment, for it and its subclasses."] [732 21 "// a custom mro() without object (typeNew refuses such a class afterwards)"] [747 28 "// bytearray's str is its repr"] [751 34 "// list___init__ and set_init ask the class of the instance"] [754 34 "// deque_iter: dequeiter_reduce gives the instance back"] [757 4 "// dict's subscript sees the subclass's instance (its __missing__; dict's accessors take the"] [758 4 "// instance through BuiltinValueHook): PY5e, part 2b"] [840 6 "// _PyObject_MaybeCallSpecialOneArg: a descriptor's AttributeError reads as no such method"] [895 4 "// slot_tp_call's _Py_EnterRecursiveCall (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's"] [896 4 "// test_recursive_call, A.__call__ = A(), overflowed Go's stack)"] [1065 1 "// reprOfInstance are the built-in types whose repr names the instance's own type (_PyType_Name(Py_TYPE(self)):"] [1066 1 "// deque's, defaultdict's): their subclasses' instances reach the Repr slot as they are, not unwrapped (PY7: a"] [1067 1 "// subclass's repr named the base)."] [1070 1 "// unwrapSlots makes a built-in base's slots work on its subclass's instances: each argument that is"] [1071 1 "// such an instance replaced by its value, and the base's __new__'s value wrapped in the instance."] [1095 16 "// an iterator's own: the instance, not its value (iter(e) is e)"] [1146 1 "// wrapNew is a built-in __new__ called for a class deriving from it: its value in an instance."] [1155 1 "// wrapInstance is the instance of the heap class t that keeps the built-in value v (wrapNew's), tracked when t"] [1156 1 "// defines __del__ (queue 218)."] [1170 26 "// socket.socket's: sock_finalize at its death"] [1175 1 "// callSpecial calls o's special method name (looked up on its type, as CPython's lookup_maybe_method)."] [1181 2 "// the C level's recursion check (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_repr_as_str,"] [1182 2 "// __repr__ = __str__ through built-in slot wrappers, overflowed Go's stack)"] [1197 1 "// callSpecialOr is callSpecial, NotImplemented when o's type has no such method."] [1206 1 "// CallSpecial calls o's special method name, found reports whether o's type has it (for the"] [1207 1 "// built-ins with no slot: __abs__, __divmod__, __round__, __format__, __reversed__ ...)."] [1217 1 "// asIndex is operator.index(o)."] [1240 1 "// objectRichCompare is object's __eq__ (identity), __ne__ (__eq__ inverted), the rest NotImplemented."] [1266 1 "// updateSubclassSlots refills the slots of t and its subclasses after a special attribute changed"] [1267 1 "// (update_slot over the subclasses: the type version tags' invalidation)."] [1278 1 "// IsSubclass is issubclass(c, cls) with __subclasscheck__; IsInstanceOf isinstance(o, cls) with"] [1279 1 "// __instancecheck__ (PyObject_IsInstance, PyObject_IsSubclass)."] [1285 3 "// \"Not a general sequence -- that opens up the road to recursion and stack overflow\" (PY7: the C"] [1286 3 "// level's check, test_isinstance's test_isinstance_recursion_limit overflowed Go's stack)"] [1339 58 "// object_issubclass's (PY7)"] [1378 1 "// checkClass is check_class: o's __bases__ a tuple, else the TypeError msg; an error other than AttributeError"] [1379 1 "// getting it raised as it is (PY7: it became the TypeError)."] [1391 1 "// abstractIsSubclass is abstract_issubclass: c's __bases__ walked, an error other than AttributeError raised"] [1392 1 "// (PY7: it was dropped), the C level's check before each recursion (test_isinstance's"] [1393 1 "// test_infinite_recursion_via_bases_tuple and test_infinite_cycle_i